  "question": {
    "text": "A small object of uniform density rolls up a curved surface with an initial velocity $v$. It reaches up to a maximum height of $\\frac{3 v^2}{4 g}$ with respect to the initial$$\n\\text { position. The object is }\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/5hO_SeRZPfuRbMzeqNADHQSXsGxc3QBbS3m0w8QuJ4E.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "RYmRT",
      "text": "\nring\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FvuT2",
      "text": "\nsolid sphere\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XWEiF",
      "text": "\nhollow sphere\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yDn5L",
      "text": "\ndisc",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} m v^2+\\frac{1}{2} I\\left(\\frac{v}{R}\\right)^2 & =m g\\left(\\frac{3 v^2}{4 g}\\right) \\\\\nI & =\\frac{1}{2} m R^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSo, body is disc.\nThe correct option is (d).",
    "image": null
  },
